mt76x2e: XR500v lab guards and counters for software TX A-MSDU layouts

With linear_tx=0 mac80211 builds A-MSDUs as frag_list skbs and mt76 hands
each skb of the list to the PDMA as a buffer of its own. mac80211 ends each
subframe on a multiple of 4 by pushing the 0-3 byte pad in front of the NEXT
skb, so after an odd-length subframe that buffer starts at an odd address.
Both BE TX DMA stalls captured on 9 Oct 2026 stopped inside such a frame, on
its last descriptor (LAST_SEC1), whose second buffer started at ...9 right
after an odd-length one. linear_tx=1 gave 0 resets in 12 phases but costs
~80 Mbit/s of download. The trigger is not isolated (odd address, odd
boundary, LAST_SEC1 on a later TXD, MPDU length), so this adds run-time
guards that remove those layouts without copying data, plus counters of
what the PDMA is actually handed. Replaces the 170 lab patch: no queue_ops
wrapper and no skb copies.

Everything is in mt76x2e.ko; mt76.ko and mt76x02-lib.ko are not touched by
this patch. Every knob defaults to the current behaviour and is writable at
run time in /sys/module/mt76x2e/parameters/:

  amsdu_no_odd=Y         refuse a subframe that would give the PDMA an odd
                         buffer address or an odd non-final buffer length
                         (mac80211 can_aggregate_in_amsdu, zero copy)
  amsdu_max_subframes=N  refuse growth past N subframes (1 = no A-MSDU)
  amsdu_max_len=N        refuse growth past an MPDU of N bytes
  amsdu_drop_odd=Y       in tx_prepare_skb, drop a multi-buffer frame that
                         still has one of those layouts, before the TXWI,
                         the packet id or the ring are touched
  amsdu_stats            read-only counters: frames by data buffers, buffer
                         start address mod 4 and 4 KiB crossings (single-
                         and multi-buffer frames), odd non-final lengths,
                         the captured shape, MPDU > 3840, refusals, drops

Proposed profile: linear_tx=0 amsdu_no_odd=1 amsdu_max_subframes=2.
Lab only, not for upstream as is.

